{%- comment -%}
  Keyword <title> backfill.

  Horizon's stock snippets/meta-tags.liquid emits `page_title`, which on a custom
  /pages/* template is just the page's name. The practical result was that the most
  important on-page ranking signal on the site read "Kilowash", "Lighting – Kilowash",
  "Testimonials – Kilowash" — brand-only titles that match none of the things a
  customer actually searches ("permanent christmas lights", "permanent lighting salt
  lake", "solar attic fan utah").

  This snippet resolves a keyword+geography title per page. It is the title twin of
  kw-seo-meta and follows the same two rules:

    1. Anything set in the Shopify admin ALWAYS wins. A page with an SEO title filled
       in is left completely alone — this snippet returns blank and the stock tag
       renders untouched. `page_title` cannot be used to detect that, because it
       silently falls back to the page name; the admin value lives in
       page.metafields.global.title_tag, so that is what gets checked.
    2. Titles are keyed on request.page_type + template.suffix, the same switch
       kw-seo-meta already uses, so the two files stay in step.

  Returns a bare string, or blank to mean "leave the stock title alone".
  Usage: {%- capture t -%}{%- render 'kw-seo-title' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  Geography note: titles are Utah-first by design. The Mid-Ohio Valley market has its
  own page and its own title; the homepage does not split its signal across three
  states, because the Google Business Profile ranks near Pleasant Grove.

  Titles are stored here rather than as theme settings deliberately: the per-template
  descriptions in kw-seo-meta are stored the same way, and a dozen more settings-panel
  text boxes would be a worse trade than one file a developer edits.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign kw_title = ''

  if request.page_type == 'index'
    comment
      On the homepage there is no metafield to check. Shopify falls page_title back to
      shop.name when no homepage SEO title is set, so an equal value means "untouched".
    endcomment
    if page_title == blank or page_title == shop.name
      assign kw_title = 'Permanent Christmas & Holiday Lights Utah | Kilowash'
    endif

  elsif request.page_type == 'page'
    unless page.metafields.global.title_tag != blank
      case template.suffix
        when 'lighting'
          assign kw_title = 'Permanent Lighting Installation | Salt Lake & Utah County'
        when 'solar'
          assign kw_title = 'Solar Attic Fans & Panel Care Utah | Kilowash'
        when 'estimate'
          assign kw_title = 'Free Permanent Lighting Estimate Utah | Kilowash'
        when 'testimonials'
          assign kw_title = 'Kilowash Reviews — Utah Lighting & Solar Installs'
        when 'about'
          assign kw_title = 'Utah Permanent Lighting & Solar Contractor | Kilowash'
        when 'contact'
          assign kw_title = 'Contact Kilowash — Permanent Lighting Utah'
        when 'mid-ohio-valley'
          comment
            Same Sept-Dec window as kw-hero-seasonal: "permanent christmas lights" is
            what Ohio Valley homeowners search in peak season.
          endcomment
          assign kw_month = 'now' | date: '%m' | plus: 0
          if kw_month >= 9
            assign kw_title = 'Permanent Christmas Lights Marietta OH & Parkersburg WV'
          else
            assign kw_title = 'Permanent Lighting — Marietta OH & Parkersburg WV'
          endif
        when 'critter-guard'
          assign kw_title = 'Pigeon & Bird Proofing for Solar Panels | Utah'
        when 'panel-cleaning'
          assign kw_title = 'Solar Panel Cleaning & Solar Care Utah | Kilowash'
        when 'city'
          comment
            City pages name the city and nothing else ("Lehi"), so the title is built
            from it rather than hardcoded — one template serves every city page.
          endcomment
          assign kw_title = 'Permanent Lighting in ' | append: page.title | append: ', UT | Kilowash'
      endcase
    endunless
  endif
-%}
{{- kw_title -}}
